---
import "../styles.css";
---

<!doctype html>
<html lang="en-AU">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8" />
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1" />
    <meta
      name="description"
      content="A clash-aware class picker. Student project, not an official ANU system. Demo timetable."
    />
    <link rel="icon" type="image/svg+xml" href="/favicon.svg" />
    <title>About — Clash-free class picker</title>
  </head>
  <body>
    <header class="site-header">
      <p class="site-title">Clash-free class picker</p>
      <p class="site-disclaimer">Student project · not an official ANU system</p>
    </header>
    <nav aria-label="site">
      <a href="/">Plan</a>
      <a href="/about">About</a>
    </nav>
    <main>
      <h1>About</h1>
      <p>
        This is a clash-aware class picker. It rebuilds one slice of ANU
        class registration (ISIS / MyTimetable): choosing which lecture,
        tutorial or crit group you go to for each course.
      </p>
      <p>
        Enrolment week is the worst week. Everyone logs in at once. The site
        slows down, keeps loading, or freezes. I still can't see all my
        class times in one place — I check lectures and tutorials against
        each other by hand, and it's easy to miss a clash. Usually I find it
        after I've picked, when the good groups are already full.
      </p>
      <p>
        Before you pick a class, hover over or tab to its Pick button. The
        week shows where it would land, as a dashed box. If it clashes, the
        class it clashes with sits beside it, and the reason is written out.
        When you have picked what matters to you, press "Fill the rest for
        me". It finds groups for every class you haven't chosen, so that
        nothing clashes, and keeps every pick you already made. If there is
        no way to do that, it saves nothing and tells you.
      </p>
      <p>Demo timetable — times are invented. Built for COMP4020 C7.</p>
    </main>
  </body>
</html>
